          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %em periodic ring spectrum
            is a
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectrum"} ring spectrum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-%E2%88%9E+ring"} A-∞ ring
            which
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} represents
            a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/periodic+cohomology+theory"} periodic cohomology theory
          %p
            A common case are the
            %em even periodic
            or
            %em 2-periodic
            ring spectra, in particular those representing
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/even+cohomology+theories"} even cohomology theories
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#PeriodicityOnModules
            Periodicity of the
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
            representing a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/periodic+ring+spectrum"} periodic ring spectrum
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension"} suspension
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/looping"} looping
            on any
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-module"} ∞-module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            is equivalent to the identity
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 2
                  %mi N
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi N
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn 2
                  %mi N
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega^2 N \simeq N \simeq \Sigma^2 N
                  \\,.
          %p
            This equivalence ought to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherence"} coherent
            to yield a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 2
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2\mathbb{Z}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} ∞-action
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-modules"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-modules
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E Mod
            (
            %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/q/46399/381"}> MO discussion
            ).
          %h3#landweber_exact_functor_theorem Landweber exact functor theorem
          %p
            There is an analogue of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Landweber+exact+functor+theorem"} Landweber exact functor theorem
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/even+cohomology+theory"} even
            2-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/periodic+cohomology+theories"}> periodic cohomology theories
            , with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MU"} MU
            replaced by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MP"} MP
            (
            %a{:href => "#HoveyStrickland99"}> Hovey-Strickland 99, theorem 2.8
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#LurieLect18"} Lurie lecture 18, prop. 11
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/even+cohomology+theory"} even
            2-periodic:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU"} KU
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MP"} MP
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+spectrum"} elliptic spectrum
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-periodic+Morava+K-theory"} 2-periodic Morava K-theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morava+E-theory"} Morava E-theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-periodic+sphere+spectrum"} 2-periodic sphere spectrum
          %h2#references References
          %p The concept of even 2-periodic multiplicative cohomology theories originates with
          %ul
            %li#AndoHopkinsStrickland
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Ando"}> Matthew Ando
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"} Michael Hopkins
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neil+Strickland"} Neil Strickland
              = succeed "," do
                %em Elliptic spectra, the Witten genus, and the theorem of the cube
          %p
            The analogue of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Landweber+exact+functor+theorem"} Landweber exact functor theorem
            for even 2-periodic cohomology is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#HoveyStrickland99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Hovey"}> Mark Hovey
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neil+Strickland"} Neil Strickland
                %em Morava K-theories and localisation
                Mem. Amer. Math. Soc., 139(666):viii+100, 1999.
            %li#LurieLect18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chromatic+Homotopy+Theory"} Chromatic Homotopy Theory
                %em Even periodic cohomology theories
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~lurie/252xnotes/Lecture18.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-graded" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebra"} supercommutative superalgebra
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
          %ul
            %li#Rezk09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Rezk"}> Charles Rezk
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The congruence criterion for power operations in Morava E-theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0902.2499"} arXiv:0902.2499
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Akhil+Mathew"}> Akhil Mathew
              , Lennart Meier, section 2.1 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em Affineness and chromatic homotopy theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1311.0514"} arXiv:1311.0514
